+# Current runtime privilege audit phases — v1
+
+Follow-up to the [actual15-statement cost](../research/crop-solar-role-sql-cost-20261019.md).
+Consolidate current catalog reads; never reuse an authorization result or
+retain a connection across audits. The original role policy, installation,
+effective privilege inquiries and all12 Solar current boundaries remain.
+
+The candidate has four read-only statements per audit:
+
+1. Database, dedicated owner, creator/object scope, role attributes/membership,
+   CONNECT, unexpected ACLs, schema/DDL/definer and sequence access. Check
+   these current facts in one SELECT with CTEs and preserve hold priority.
+   Return the same discovered relation/routine identities for the matrices.
+2. The existing full table/grant-option mismatch query, unchanged.
+3. The existing table/column/grant-option mismatch query, unchanged and fresh.
+4. Current routine execution and creator defaults, retaining hold priority.
+
+Each SELECT reads current server data. This does not assert a transaction-wide
+snapshot under Read Committed. Keep the separate matrices and their current
+NULL-aware checks so revocation or object deletion after discovery or between
+the matrices still fails closed. No SQL mutations, new functions, schema changes,
+new dependencies, numerical/worker changes or timing/cap increases are included.
+
+Acceptance: at most four actual audit statements, each successful matrix still
+returns zero rows, identical policy metadata and existing holds; selected and
+unselected storage and all existing NOLOGIN/SCRAM role-hardening regression
+tests pass. Include actual between-statement changes, current farm/source rights
+and normal/hold result query regression. Measure the same owned component in
+paired order with the original implementation; do not infer native throughput
+from an isolated timing. Preserve5root/descendants, source/HTML/originals,
+512MiB/PID/1GiB combined and complete owned resource cleanup.
+
+The use of CTEs and statement snapshots follows PostgreSQL16 documentation on
+[WITH](https://www.postgresql.org/docs/16/queries-with.html),
+[privilege inquiries](https://www.postgresql.org/docs/16/functions-info.html#FUNCTIONS-INFO-ACCESS-TABLE)
+and [Read Committed](https://www.postgresql.org/docs/16/transaction-iso.html).
+The grouping and acceptance criteria are project design decisions. Actual farm
+data/rights, G0–G4, original native64-step success and deployment remain separate.
